---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="About · Brett Boggs" description="Operator turned builder. St. Louis.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <p class="eyebrow">03</p>
    <h1>About</h1>
    <p class="lede">Operator turned builder. St.&nbsp;Louis.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="opener">
    <div class="prose opener-copy">
      <p>
        I spent a decade running physical operations before I ever shipped software. Service
        lane at a Honda dealership. General manager of a car wash, then a group of them, then a
        district. Operations for a real estate investment company. Years of schedules, payroll,
        equipment that breaks on the coldest day of the year, and customers standing in front of
        you expecting an answer.
      </p>
      <p>
        That decade is the point. Most software for real-world businesses is built by people who
        have never run one, and it shows: tools that demand data entry nobody has time for,
        reports that answer questions nobody asked, five systems where one should be. I got
        tired of being the operator those tools were inflicted on, so I became the person who
        builds them instead.
      </p>
    </div>
    <figure class="portrait">
      <span class="portrait-plate">
        <img src="/about/brett.jpg" alt="Brett Boggs" width="880" height="1121" loading="eager" />
      </span>
      <figcaption>For once, the wrong side of the camera</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      Now I co-found and build <a href="/work/datum/">Datum</a>, one system for running a
      construction company. I am the sole engineer: design, frontend, backend, security,
      infrastructure, and the AI underneath, end to end. The
      <a href="/work/datum/">case study</a> has the numbers, and the decision logs under it
      have the honest version: what was chosen, what it cost, what broke.
    </p>
    <p>
      The same instinct runs through everything here. <a href="/work/apparent-low/">Apparent
      Low</a> exists because extraction you can't measure is extraction you can't trust. The
      <a href="/work/photography/">photography</a> is the same discipline pointed at light
      instead of systems. The <a href="/lab/">Lab</a> is where things get tried before they
      earn a place.
    </p>
    <p>
      I work best on problems where the software has to survive contact with a real operation:
      a foreman's morning, a month-end close, a bid due at 10 a.m. If that is the kind of
      problem you have, I want to hear about it.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section class="reach">
    <p class="reach-head">Reach me</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <span class="reach-label">Email</span>
        <a href="mailto:brettmboggs@gmail.com">brettmboggs@gmail.com</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="reach-label">LinkedIn</span>
        <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brettmboggs/" rel="noopener">linkedin.com/in/brettmboggs</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="reach-label">GitHub</span>
        <a href="https://github.com/brettmboggs" rel="noopener">github.com/brettmboggs</a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <span class="reach-label">Datum</span>
        <a href="https://datumci.com" rel="noopener">datumci.com</a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <a class="back-link" href="/">&larr; Home</a>
</Base>

<style>
  /* magazine-profile opener: copy left, printed plate right */
  .opener {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(18rem, 3fr) minmax(14rem, 2fr);
    gap: 2.8rem;
    align-items: start;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .opener-copy {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  /* the portrait as a plate printed in the site's own ink: a warm sienna
     duotone that develops to full color under the cursor, like a print coming
     up in the tray. pure filter chain, so the development animates. */
  .portrait {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .portrait-plate {
    display: block;
    border: 1px solid var(--paper-deep);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .portrait img {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    filter: grayscale(1) sepia(0.55) hue-rotate(-12deg) saturate(1.6) contrast(1.04) brightness(1.03);
    transition: filter 0.7s var(--ease-warm);
  }
  .portrait:hover img,
  .portrait:focus-within img {
    filter: none;
  }
  .portrait figcaption {
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.72rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .opener {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: 2rem;
    }
    .portrait {
      max-width: 19rem;
      order: -1;
    }
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .portrait img {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
  .reach {
    margin-top: 4rem;
    padding-top: 1.6rem;
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .reach-head {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
  .reach ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 1.2rem 0 0;
    padding: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }
  .reach li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 6rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    align-items: baseline;
  }
  .reach-label {
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: 0.78rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }
</style>
